      "customfield_10012" : "0|i004fz:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Allow WriteOnlyProperty<> setter to be overloaded.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Not sure how practical this is, given the need to EITHER package the two overloads in one function object, or have the setter function object take T, ... parameter (not sure hwo ti find out what passed in ...).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Use case is ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Frameworks::WebServer::Response object and the SetContentSizePolicy method. this would make sense to use  properties, but cannot beacuse we have two overloads (where we dtake csp or scp/size>. ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "MAYBE the right way to think about this is to make the property value be tuple>ContentPolicySize, uint64_t>? That would address this use case as well. MAYBE smarter.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
